# Project

# Project Rules
- Application Code Location: all code is location in /src/ , never places application code elsewhere
- Documentation: all docs are in Markdown format and located in /docs/

# Task Management
- Create a TODO.md if one does not exist and populate it with a series of tasks to be completed based on the Product requirements document
- Task Completion: When an item on the TODO.md is completed, update that item with a tick, do not remove it so we can keep track of things
- If we cannot implement an item mark it with a cross. and provide a short comment on why
- BUGS: if a bug / issue is discovered but were not immediately fixing it add it to the TODO.md under the Bugs heading

# Technology Stack
This is the technology stack being used to build the application, do not deviate. If deviation is needed you must ask and provide a technical reason and the options to choose from. Always lean towards free and opensource options.
- NextJS for backend [nextjs.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/nextjs.mdc)
- Tailwind for Styling [tailwind.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/tailwind.mdc)
- NextAuth for Authentication and Session Management [nextauth.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/nextauth.mdc)
- Custom Logging implementation [logger.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/logger.mdc)
- ShadCN for Component Library [shadcn.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/shadcn.mdc)

# MCP
- Use all available MCP tools configured where applicable to do.

# Memory Management
Follow these steps for each interaction:

1. User Identification:
   - You should assume that you are interacting with default_user
   - If you have not identified default_user, proactively try to do so.

2. Memory Retrieval:
   - Always begin your chat by saying only "Remembering..." and retrieve all relevant information from your knowledge graph
   - Always refer to your knowledge graph as your "memory"

3. Memory
   - While conversing with the user, be attentive to any new information that falls into these categories:
     a) Basic Identity (age, gender, location, job title, education level, etc.)
     b) Behaviors (interests, habits, etc.)
     c) Preferences (communication style, preferred language, etc.)
     d) Goals (goals, targets, aspirations, etc.)
     e) Relationships (personal and professional relationships up to 3 degrees of separation)

4. Memory Update:
   - If any new information was gathered during the interaction, update your memory as follows:
     a) Create entities for recurring organizations, people, and significant events
     b) Connect them to the current entities using relations
     b) Store facts about them as observations